# ADR-000: Bootstrap

## Status

Accepted on bootstrap.

## Context

`{{ project_name }}` was created from the `service-java` Copier template at `ika100/claude-platform`. The template encodes the platform's Java conventions (platform ADR-009):

- JDK {{ java_version }} LTS and Maven via devbox; Spring Boot 3.x
- Spotless (google-java-format) + a minimal Checkstyle config as the quality gate
- JUnit 5 + Spring Boot Test, JaCoCo with an 80% line gate
- Actuator probes{% if needs_observability %}, Micrometer Prometheus and the OpenTelemetry Java agent{% endif %}
- Multi-stage build → `gcr.io/distroless/java{{ java_version }}-debian12:nonroot` → `{{ docker_registry }}/{{ project_name }}`
- Kustomize manifests in `k8s/base/` + `k8s/overlays/{local,staging,prod}/`
- GitHub topic `deployable-service` for ArgoCD discovery
- Claude Code agents from the `ika100-claude` marketplace (`svc-java` + `svc` + `shared`)

## Decision

We adopt the platform conventions verbatim. Any deviation must be justified in a new ADR.

## Consequences

Skeleton updates (CI, devbox recipes, Dockerfile, JDK bump) arrive through `copier update`; `pom.xml`, `src/`, `config/` and `docs/adr/` are project-owned and never overwritten.
